course: dictionary
lesson: 5347
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Killing can mean causing something to die, but it can also mean very funny or very painful. The words around it show you which meaning the writer wants. This is context.
explain: In a science lesson, «soap is killing bacteria» means the soap destroys germs. Bacteria are tiny living things, so killing here means making them die. The science topic is the clue.
explain: Slang works differently. «You're killing me!» after a joke means «You're so funny». But «My feet are killing me» after a long walk means they hurt a lot. The feeling in the sentence tells you whether it is laughter or pain.
explain: In the news, killing is a serious word. «War means killing and destruction» means people die because of war. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Killing can be a verb (to kill), a noun (a killing) or an adjective (a killing pace).
fact: Killing means causing someone or something to die.
fact: In the news, a killing means a death caused on purpose.
fact: To make a killing means to make a lot of money quickly. This is informal.
fact: «You're killing me!» can mean «You're so funny» or «You're annoying me». «My feet are killing me» means they hurt a lot.
exercise: In a science lesson, «soap is killing bacteria». What does killing mean here? | Washing a dirty floor | Feeling very happy | *Destroying tiny germs | Playing a game
exercise: Sam laughs and says, «You're killing me!» after a joke. What does he mean? | You have made me sad | You are hurting me by pushing | *You're so funny | You owe me money
exercise: «My feet are killing me» after a long hike. What does it mean? | They are sleepy and want to nap | They are very clean | *They hurt a lot | They are cold and wet
test: In the news, what does a killing mean? | A fun game at school | *A death caused on purpose | A fast run around the park | A loud cheer after a goal
test: What does «to make a killing» mean? | To cook a big dinner | To tell a long story | To win a fight | *To make a lot of money quickly
exam: Read «War means killing and destruction.» What does killing mean here? | Cleaning up a mess | Playing a funny game | Making a lot of money | *Causing people to die
